  "summary": "A fresco painting method where artists complete sections in single day sessions separated by visible seams.",
  "description": "Characterized by distinct day-joint lines between sections painted in separate sessions, this technique emerged from practical constraints of plaster drying time. Developed during Italian Renaissance masters like Giotto and Michelangelo used this method to manage large-scale fresco projects.",
